<title>UK: CalEnergy's Northern Electric yr profits down.</title>
<headline>CalEnergy's Northern Electric yr profits down.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Electric Plc, acquired by CalEnergy Co Inc of the United States at the end of last year, said on Tuesday its pretax profit for the year to March 31 was 103 million stg, down from 150.8 million previously.  </p>
<p>The profits came on turnover of 954.1 million stg compared with 902.2 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>Northern said its prices were further reduced and are now 25 pct lower than five years ago in real terms, while capital spending on its electricity network increased by 16 pct to 58.6 million.</p>
<p>Electricity units distributed were up 1.4 pct on the previous year.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
